VeridianOS: declare variables at the start of their blocks

GCC reported "ISO C90 forbids mixed declarations and code
[-Wdeclaration-after-statement]" (the package's own warning flags) at
icccm/icccm.c:344, 353, 755 and at ewmh.c:605, 615, 623, 761, 1232, 1320,
1452. ewmh.c is generated by m4 from ewmh/ewmh.c.m4, so that is the file
changed here (the build regenerates ewmh.c from it).

Each declaration moved to the top of its function; where it had an
initializer, the initialization stays where it was as an assignment, so
the order of evaluation is unchanged. In xcb_ewmh_init_atoms() the
iterator's separate initialization is dropped because the for statement
right after it initializes it again with the same value. No behaviour
change.

